(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #112 — before the fix, falling off the end of a
 map-returning function left the caller reading a bogus map header off
 whatever rax last held, which walked as an unbounded (or garbage-sized)
 map and hung on `'s length`. The fixed epilogue allocates a real, fresh
 empty map, exactly as `{}` does, so it reports its length and still
 takes a key set.)

